    verification guardPoolDispatchesLongestFirstImplementGate : Test { :>> id = "76afcedb-d9d9-4601-9745-42e0da94af8b"; :>> title = "Sprint 657 implement gate"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-10"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Built: guards.rs dispatch_order (stable sort by Reverse(receipt ms), untimed first), DURATIONS mutex filled in note_critical_path and cleared per run_in_parallel, last_durations(); receipt.rs StoredGuard.ms (serde default) filled from last_durations in record_green, durations(root) reader; three unit tests. Seeded the receipt (68 of 69 guards timed). Measured three runs each way: 2147-2252 ms before, 2600-2991 ms after, guard sum 16.9 -> 28.0 s, git x40 3977 -> 9404 ms - and wrote 'slower' into the code comment. Then the same declaration-order code, rebuilt, measured 2853-3039 ms: the host had moved thirty percent with no code change (13 stale kernel JVMs swept, Defender at the top of CPU). Added an env-gated longest-first to one binary (keel-ab.exe, source restored before anything else was touched) and ran six interleaved pairs: 2567 vs 2544 ms medians, no difference inside the spread; under longest-first the longest guard itself stretched 1.6 -> 2.2 s and git x40 5.2 -> 7.3 s. Reverted: dispatch_order and receipt::durations removed, run_all comment states the A/B and the mechanism, the three dispatch tests replaced by last_durations_names_every_guard_that_ran (placed above the run_all test's doc comment, not between the comment and its #[test] - the sprint 655 slip), ms kept in the receipt. Probe script: docstring states what measurement found, --real's verdict names its independence assumption, --ab summarises two interleaved sets and REFUSES two sets whose mtimes do not interleave (probed: alternating accepted, two blocks refused; the refusal fired on this sprint's own before/after files). CLAUDE.md section 5 states the order and why. D0431 recorded (proposed). issue458 recorded in-field with D0431 as resolver. Final binary rebuilt from the restored source: KEEL_GUARD_LPT=1 prints no TEMP-AB line."; }
